    "title": "1973 BMW 3.0 CSL 3.2L",
    "summary": "This 1973 BMW 3.0 CSL is one of 1,265 homologation specials built between 1971 and 1975, and it is one of 110 late-1973, left-hand-drive Coupés powered by a fuel-injected 3.2L inline-six paired with a four-speed manual transmission. Of the 110, this is one of the 76 that were specified in Polaris Metallic, and it is further equipped with the \"Batmobile\" Aero Package, 14\" light-alloy turbine wheels, Sheel sport seats, and a three-spoke wheel. Chassis 2275478 was manufactured on the 17th September 1973 and was delivered later that month in Essen, Germany. The car was imported in 2001 to the UK and thereafter underwent two phases of restoration that saw a rebuild of the engine along with body refurbishment, overhauling the brakes and suspension, and renewing the undercarriage with a lacquered finish. Previously modified with Alpina parts and a triple Weber intake, the engine has been returned to a more stock configuration with a rebuilt fuel-injection system along with a re-sleeved block. The gearbox has also been rebuilt, and the clutch was replaced as well. Featured in Classic Car in 2007 and acquired by the selling dealer in 2025, this E9 CSL is now offered in the UK with service records and V5C registration.",
